# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supported file types {#supported-file-types}"
msgstr "Tipe file yang didukung {#supported-file-types}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow checks the contents of each uploaded file, not its extension, and rejects files of other types:\n"
msgstr "Managed workflow memeriksa isi setiap file yang diunggah, bukan ekstensinya, dan menolak file dengan tipe lain:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Accepted | Rejected |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| JSON, plain text, YAML, and Python files; binary files such as NumPy (`.npy`, `.npz`), QPY, and pickle files; tar, gzip, and zip archives | CSV, PNG, PDF, HDF5, and empty files |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Diterima | Ditolak |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| File JSON, teks biasa, YAML, dan Python; file biner seperti NumPy (`.npy`, `.npz`), QPY, dan pickle; arsip tar, gzip, dan zip | File CSV, PNG, PDF, HDF5, dan file kosong |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: let's figure out if this is recent, and what the file size limitation actually is (50 MB?) */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "File names {#file-names}"
msgstr "Nama file {#file-names}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Use only letters, digits, underscores (`_`), hyphens (`-`), and periods (`.`).** A managed workflow removes other characters, such as spaces, from the name when you download or delete a file. For example, you can upload `my results.json`, but you cannot download it.\n"
msgstr "**Pakai hanya huruf, angka, underscore (`_`), tanda hubung (`-`), dan titik (`.`).** Managed workflow menghapus karakter lain, seperti spasi, dari nama saat kamu mengunduh atau menghapus file. Misalnya, kamu bisa mengunggah `my results.json`, tetapi tidak bisa mengunduhnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**File storage has no folders.** `file_upload()` keeps only the file name, so `inputs/params.json` is stored as `params.json`.\n"
msgstr "**File storage tidak punya folder.** `file_upload()` hanya menyimpan nama file, jadi `inputs/params.json` disimpan sebagai `params.json`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: upload does not sanitize file names, but download and delete do (gateway/api/utils.py sanitize_file_name()). Confirm whether upload should reject or sanitize these names. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read files in a workflow {#read-files-in-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Baca file di workflow {#read-files-in-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the name of the file when you run the workflow:\n"
msgstr "Berikan nama file saat kamu menjalankan workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, edit your workflow code to read the file from `/function_user_data`, which is where every job sees file storage:\n"
msgstr "Supaya ini bisa jalan, ubah kode workflow-mu untuk membaca file dari `/function_user_data`, yaitu tempat setiap job melihat file storage:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inside a job, read and write files through this folder. The client file methods, such as `file_upload()` and `file_download()`, are for your local notebook.\n"
msgstr "Di dalam job, baca dan tulis file lewat folder ini. Method file klien, seperti `file_upload()` dan `file_download()`, ditujukan untuk notebook lokalmu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To read an archive, extract it to the local disk:\n"
msgstr "Untuk membaca arsip, ekstrak ke disk lokal:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write temporary files to `/tmp`. File storage is object storage that the job sees as a folder, so file storage is slower than the local disk. Do heavy reads and writes on the local disk, and copy finished files to file storage.\n"
msgstr "Tulis file sementara ke `/tmp`. File storage adalah object storage yang dilihat job sebagai folder, jadi file storage lebih lambat daripada disk lokal. Lakukan pembacaan dan penulisan yang berat di disk lokal, lalu salin file yang sudah selesai ke file storage.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm how the mount behaves for appends, renames, and partial writes, and how soon a file that one job writes is visible to a job that is running at the same time. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save output files {#save-output-files}"
msgstr "Simpan file output {#save-output-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Your local notebook reads the names of the output files from the result:\n"
msgstr "Notebook lokalmu membaca nama file output dari hasilnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, save each output file at the top level of `/function_user_data`, and return the file names with `save_result()`:\n"
msgstr "Supaya ini bisa jalan, simpan setiap file output di level teratas `/function_user_data`, dan kembalikan nama file dengan `save_result()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Files that the job writes outside `/function_user_data`, such as in `/tmp` or the current folder, are deleted when the job ends.\n"
msgstr "File yang ditulis job di luar `/function_user_data`, seperti di `/tmp` atau folder saat ini, dihapus saat job berakhir.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm that the mount stores /function_user_data/<folder>/<file> as the storage key .../data/<folder>/<file>, so that later jobs can read subfolders. file_download() can't fetch these files: sanitize_file_name() strips \"/\", and files() lists only the base name (file_storage_fleets.py get_public_files()). */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download output files {#download-output-files}"
msgstr "Unduh file output {#download-output-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the job ends, download each file with `file_download()`. Set `target_name` to choose the local file name, and `download_location` to choose an existing local folder:\n"
msgstr "Setelah job berakhir, unduh setiap file dengan `file_download()`. Atur `target_name` untuk memilih nama file lokal, dan `download_location` untuk memilih folder lokal yang sudah ada:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Without `target_name`, `file_download()` adds a random prefix to the local file name, such as `downloaded_3f2a9c1b_energies.npy`, and returns the name that it used.\n"
msgstr "Tanpa `target_name`, `file_download()` menambahkan prefiks acak ke nama file lokal, seperti `downloaded_3f2a9c1b_energies.npy`, dan mengembalikan nama yang dipakainya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download many outputs as one archive {#download-many-outputs-as-one-archive}"
msgstr "Unduh banyak output sebagai satu arsip {#download-many-outputs-as-one-archive}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a job saves many output files, or files in subfolders, bundle them into one archive in the workflow, and download only the archive:\n"
msgstr "Kalau job menyimpan banyak file output, atau file di subfolder, kemas semuanya menjadi satu arsip di workflow, dan unduh arsipnya saja:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, write the outputs to a folder on the local disk, add the folder to an archive in `/tmp`, and copy the archive to file storage:\n"
msgstr "Supaya ini bisa jalan, tulis output ke folder di disk lokal, tambahkan folder itu ke arsip di `/tmp`, lalu salin arsipnya ke file storage:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the archive is built on the local disk and copied in one step, file storage never holds an incomplete archive. The archive keeps the folder structure, and it can contain files of any type. In this example, the files are extracted to `outputs/<run_name>/`.\n"
msgstr "Karena arsip dibuat di disk lokal dan disalin dalam satu langkah, file storage tidak pernah menyimpan arsip yang belum lengkap. Arsip mempertahankan struktur folder, dan bisa berisi file dengan tipe apa pun. Dalam contoh ini, file diekstrak ke `outputs/<run_name>/`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Delete files {#delete-files}"
msgstr "Hapus file {#delete-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow does not delete files from file storage, so files remain until you delete them with `file_delete()`:\n"
msgstr "Managed workflow tidak menghapus file dari file storage, jadi file tetap ada sampai kamu menghapusnya dengan `file_delete()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`file_delete()` reports success even if the file does not exist, so check the name with `files()` first. To delete all the files of one run, filter `files()` by the run's name prefix, as described in the next section:\n"
msgstr "`file_delete()` melaporkan berhasil meskipun file-nya tidak ada, jadi cek dulu namanya dengan `files()`. Untuk menghapus semua file dari satu run, filter `files()` berdasarkan awalan nama run, seperti dijelaskan di bagian berikutnya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: on Fleets, deleting a missing file returns \"Requested file was deleted.\" because gateway/core/ibm_cloud/cos/cos_client.py delete_object() treats a missing key as deleted. Confirm whether file_delete() should return 404 instead. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: give each run's files a unique name {#best-practice-give-each-runs-files-a-unique-name}"
msgstr "Praktik terbaik: beri setiap file run nama yang unik {#best-practice-give-each-runs-files-a-unique-name}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All of your runs of a workflow share the same file storage, and a file that a job saves replaces any stored file with the same name. If you start several runs at the same time and each run saves `energies.npy`, only the last one is kept.\n"
msgstr "Semua run dari satu workflow memakai penyimpanan file yang sama, dan file yang disimpan oleh sebuah job akan menggantikan file tersimpan mana pun dengan nama yang sama. Kalau kamu memulai beberapa run sekaligus dan tiap run menyimpan `energies.npy`, hanya yang terakhir yang tersimpan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a best practice, pass a run name as an argument, and start the name of every file that the run saves with it:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai praktik terbaik, kirim nama run sebagai argumen, dan awali nama setiap file yang disimpan run itu dengan nama tersebut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All runs can read the same input file, `hamiltonian.npz`, because they only read it. Upload a shared input one time, before you start the runs.\n"
msgstr "Semua run bisa membaca file input yang sama, `hamiltonian.npz`, karena mereka hanya membacanya. Unggah input bersama satu kali saja, sebelum kamu memulai run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use run names that you can recognize later, and that contain only letters, digits, underscores, hyphens, and periods. With one prefix for each run, you can find, download, and [delete](#delete-files) the files of a run together.\n"
msgstr "Pakai nama run yang mudah kamu kenali nanti, dan hanya berisi huruf, angka, garis bawah, tanda hubung, dan titik. Dengan satu awalan untuk tiap run, kamu bisa menemukan, mengunduh, dan [menghapus](#delete-files) file dari satu run sekaligus.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: checkpoint long jobs {#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs}"
msgstr "Praktik terbaik: buat checkpoint untuk job yang panjang {#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A job that is canceled, fails, or reaches the 24-hour limit loses everything that is not in file storage. For long runs, save a checkpoint to file storage at regular intervals, and resume from it when you run the workflow again with the same run name:\n"
msgstr "Job yang dibatalkan, gagal, atau mencapai batas 24 jam akan kehilangan semua yang tidak ada di penyimpanan file. Untuk run yang panjang, simpan checkpoint ke penyimpanan file secara berkala, lalu lanjutkan dari situ saat kamu menjalankan workflow lagi dengan nama run yang sama:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To continue a run that stopped, call `run()` again with the same arguments.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melanjutkan run yang berhenti, panggil `run()` lagi dengan argumen yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the following points in mind:\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan poin-poin berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Write the checkpoint to the local disk first, and then copy it.** If the job stops during a write, the stored checkpoint is incomplete, and the next run cannot read it.\n"
msgstr "**Tulis checkpoint ke disk lokal dulu, baru salin.** Kalau job berhenti saat menulis, checkpoint yang tersimpan jadi tidak lengkap, dan run berikutnya tidak bisa membacanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Choose an interval that matches the cost of a step.** Save often enough that you do not lose much work, but not so often that writing checkpoints slows the job.\n"
msgstr "**Pilih interval yang sesuai dengan biaya satu langkah.** Simpan cukup sering supaya tidak banyak pekerjaan yang hilang, tapi jangan terlalu sering sampai penulisan checkpoint memperlambat job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Delete checkpoints after the run succeeds.** A later run with the same name then starts from the beginning.\n"
msgstr "**Hapus checkpoint setelah run berhasil.** Run berikutnya dengan nama yang sama akan mulai dari awal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a job that is canceled, you can also save partial results in a [`SIGTERM` handler](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"
msgstr "Untuk job yang dibatalkan, kamu juga bisa menyimpan hasil parsial di [handler `SIGTERM`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah berikutnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Run a parameter sweep](/guides/run-parameter-sweep) to start one job for each input.\n"
"- [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors) to save partial results when a job is canceled.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Rekomendasi\">\n"
"- [Jalankan parameter sweep](/guides/run-parameter-sweep) untuk memulai satu job untuk setiap input.\n"
"- [Tulis log dan tangani error](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors) untuk menyimpan hasil parsial saat job dibatalkan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
